  "id": "genetic-counseling",
  "term": "genetic counseling",
  "definition": "Genetic counseling is an educational process in which people or families receive information, guidance, and usually psychosocial support about a genetic condition that may affect them. It is intended to help them make informed choices about reproduction and other health-related decisions using information about the condition, testing options, and management approaches.",
